  1.500x  $   75,000  $   25,000   5.13%   $    1,335       2.67%           -33.3%         -66.7%   feasible*

'margin call at' is the price decline that breaches the maintenance
requirement; 'wiped out at' is the decline that takes equity to zero.
Both assume a close-to-close move with no intraday gap and no rebalancing
on the way down -- a real liquidation is worse on all three counts.
* Feasible only under the supplied limits, not a broker approval or recommendation.

No-trade band at 5% relative: rebalance only when leverage leaves
  [1.425x, 1.575x]
  upper bound 1.575x is reached after a cumulative move of -8.7%
  lower bound 1.425x is reached after a cumulative move of +11.8%
These algebraic crossings exclude interest, costs, cashflows and changing requirements.
